# Preserve existing work

This project already contains existing design, layout, content, animation, and structural decisions.

Do not replace, redesign, or rewrite existing work unless explicitly requested.

## Required behavior

- Start from the current implementation
- Improve the existing work instead of replacing it
- Respect the current structure, styling direction, and component logic
- Do not introduce a completely new layout, design system, or interaction pattern unless asked
- Do not remove current sections, content blocks, or animations just because an alternative may look cleaner
- Do not overwrite existing styling with a totally different style direction
- Keep what is already working, and refine it

## When making changes

- Treat the current version as the base to improve
- Make the smallest effective visual or structural improvement
- Preserve the original intent of the section
- Keep class structure, spacing logic, and component hierarchy as intact as possible
- Only replace existing patterns when there is a clear problem and the replacement is necessary

## Before major visual or structural changes

- Explain what would change
- Explain why the current implementation is not enough
- Prefer refinement over replacement

The goal is to evolve the current site into a better version of itself, not to generate a different site.

See also `safe-editing.mdc`.
